  "notes": [
    "naive_no_clamp_simulation = what a full-canvas blur + card matte would produce (wrong method); it is only a numeric reference showing the red would bleed in.",
    "b was selected by the smallest mean_abs_diff in card_inner_no_edge (inner card, 40 px border excluded).",
    "The full 4-value sweep and the A/B clamp comparison are stored in this file and the AE project keeps all variant comps (04_AB_Variants) plus the A/B blur comps for inspection.",
    "AE radius convention (from the earlier calibration): Fast Box Blur iterations=2, radius b produces a tent kernel w(k)=(W-|k|)/W^2 with W=2b+1 and non-zero half-support H=2b. Figma's tent for R=40 is matched by b=19.5 (H=39..40 px), consistent with Figma's large-radius 0.96-0.97 R measurement."
  ],
